<title>GERMANY: TABLE - German July adjusted jobless rises 17,000.</title>
<headline>TABLE - German July adjusted jobless rises 17,000.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Labour Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p>PAN-GERMAN UNEMPLOYMENT</p>
<p>				 July 97	 June 97	  July 96</p>
<p> Number (unadj)	    4.354 million     4.222 million	3.912 million</p>
<p> Number (adj)		4.396 million     4.379 million	3.942 million</p>
<p> Change (adj)	     +17,000	  +14,000	  +15,000</p>
<p> Rate (unadj)		11.4 pct	11.0 pct	 10.2 pct</p>
<p> Short-time workers	128,318	 167,668	  225,123</p>
<p> Vacancies		   355,683	 366,897	  348,934</p>
<p>Change in number in work May 97	  Apr 97</p>
<p>				 -25,000	 -39,000</p>
<p>NOTE - Numbers in work data refer to change from previous month. Details on numbers in work to be released later today.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
